- The inlined python block, fixtures, and assertions are verbatim-loadable and were verified to work end-to-end (patched copies and the full suite passed) — no hallucinated symbols, no quoting hazards (the block contains no single quotes to clash with the `python3 -c '...'` wrapper), and the de-indentation instructions are explicit and correct.
- Outstanding boundary-contract coverage: the new reason strings, the single-line guarantee, the no-PII invariant, and the schema-drift path are all exercised through the real production path (fixture server → curl → python → stdout → grep), not shape tests.
- Precise anchors everywhere (method names, `frames_rc`/`frames` shell semantics, `check_failure`, `event_latest` 999-branch) — nothing line-number-bound.
- The `metadata()` reuse claim for issues 222/333 was verified true (the fixture server serves any numeric id), so the fixture insertions need no server-side changes.
